awareness and expression therapy, which was developed by Mark Lumley, who is a psychologist at Wayne State University, who had sort of over the course of decades built up towards this amazing intervention. And it has gone a bit of a radical direction in terms of how we treat pain. And one thing that it's done that's very different is it a true. It addresses trauma. It addresses historical experiences of life trauma, adverse life events, even experiences of discrimination or stigma. So whereas some of the CBT and the CBT-based treatments kind of came in saying, well, let's talk about what's going on in your life now, the past isn't important because we want to kind of stay symptom focused and focused on the here

