So my colleagues and I actually just completed a systematic review of the last 10 years of research studies measuring depression and anxiety and chronic pain. So we identified hundreds of studies, hundreds of thousands of participants. And we found that number to be a around 40%. So around 40% of people who have chronic pain also have depression or have anxiety. So, you know, we know that rates are high. So we know that this co-occurrence is common. The co-occurrence of pain and depression or pain and anxiety is common. But some other things we now know or not everybody has these co-occurring conditions, right? Many people live really high functioning lives with chronic pain and it doesn't affect their mood. But for a lot of people with pain, depression is high. And we're still trying to figure out how to treat that particular

18
