from the studies that we do have is that those relationships are bidirectional. So sometimes chronic pain precedes depression and anxiety, and sometimes depression and anxiety, precedes chronic pain. And I think that where we will go next is understanding how that might be different for different types of chronic pain conditions. So one of the reasons I became interested in this topic was I myself was experiencing chronic pain. And you just talked about the link between depression and pain. Now, I was not depressed, but one of the treatments that was prescribed for me was an antidepressant, duloxatine was given to me. And I have to say it didn't do anything for me. I wasn't depressed, so I didn't feel happier, but it did nothing for my pain. So what is

