going on with these antidepressants and pain? How are they changing people's experience of pain? Yeah. Thank you for sharing that. And I'm sorry to hear that you were sort of prescribed something that came with plenty of side effects and wasn't helpful to you in the end. And so in general, we don't know a lot about sort of the best course of treatment. So we sort of have these treatments as a laundry list of treatments, but we're not as the science is not at a state that we know that this particular treatment works best for this particular pain condition and this particular type of person. So, you know, it's a bit like throwing a dart on a dart on a dart board. You know, you kind of try what you can. So antidepressant medications are considered a frontline treatment

