pain, didn't do a thing. How effective is acupuncture in treating chronic pain? The evidence is quite mixed and partly that's because there haven't been a ton of high quality research studies in this area. But I think overall we could say minimally effective, but important caveat compared to active control. So if you give one group of people acupuncture and you give one group of people nothing, people who get acupuncture will feel better than the people who got nothing. If you compare sort of real acupuncture to like sham acupuncture, so you sort of hook some needles, but not necessarily, you know, the way that acupuncture is supposed to be delivered,

